00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.110
<b>Saitama University</b>

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.110
<b>BAM</b>

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.110
<b>THUD</b>

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:40.840
Himuro.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.610
You're three minutes late.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.510
Two minutes, thirty-two seconds.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.530
If you're specializing in 
science and engineering,

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.910
you need to be precise about time,

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:49.990
Yukimura-kun.

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:51.170
Hmph.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:55.260
Save the backtalk for after you've 
made up the three minutes' work.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.090
Serves as the perfect handicap 
for me, don't you think?

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.650
Oh, by the way, Yukimura-kun.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:00.950
What is it, Himuro?

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:05.030
I am in l—

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.450
Luh?

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.840
L—... L—...

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.010
...luv wiv you!

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:15.780
Wow! Our senpai really 
did become a manga!

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:18.280
Proof 5
Science-types Fell in Love, 
So They Tried Analyzing Their Proof of Love.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.520
So this is how she 
confessed her feelings.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.540
There are some parts that 
are a little different.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.030
In the history of my manga, 
it's by far the most popular!

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.540
An anime adaptation might 
not be just a dream!

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.530
Being turned into a manga like this...

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.700
it's embarrassing, isn't it?

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.540
It's for the purpose of gathering 
"proof of love" data from the readers.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.420
We have no choice.

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:39.800
If that were not the case...

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.540
I would never work with that manga artist.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.440
Since the Okinawa training camp,

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.640
Yukimura-senpai's been even 
harsher on Yamamoto-senpai.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.160
Did something happen?

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.810
I-I don't know.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.010
And you.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.510
If you have time to play around like that,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.070
then hurry up and hand over 
the data you've collected.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.810
Now, now. Please, there's no need to panic.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.090
I've asked my editor to bring over 
the compiled data. It's coming now.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:10.340
An editor? That's just 
like a real manga artist!

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.400
You've reached an impressive 
status, haven't you?

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.830
To think you can order editors around.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.620
"Order around"? You make me sound terrible!

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:22.290
I made a deal in exchange for 
my work on my manuscript.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.680
I just said, "Won't you please 
take care of compiling the data?"

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.350
So, did you finish your manuscript?

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.860
Of course I didn't!

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.460
And that's why you ran away, isn't it?

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.480
Exactly!

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.730
My editor doesn't know about this place yet.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.200
It's my sanctuary!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:39.850
Huh?

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.550
Who could that be?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.500
Yeah? I'm coming!

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:49.620
Kosuke-san! Don't open the door!

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.060
May I ask who you are?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.380
Yamamoto's Editor
<b>Ogu-san
</b>Height: 182 cm
Former Rugby Player

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.380
m 0 0 l 222 0 l 220 140 l 0 140

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.290
U-Um... Might you possibly 
have come to the wrong place?

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.020
Yamamoto-sensei.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:16.110
Yamamoto-senpai! This is the fifth floor!

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.630
We're on the fifth floor!

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.930
Please, let go of me!

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.080
If I'm going to be torn into shreds of meat,

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:24.010
I'd rather have compound 
fractures all over my body!

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.080
Sensei.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.600
Your deadline passed long ago.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.410
You've drawn your manga, haven't you?

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:35.540
I will! I will! 
Just don't lock me in that room!

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:44.550
Being a manga artist is a 
difficult job, isn't it?

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.290
She's only reaping what she sowed.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:50.530
Still, once you get Yamamoto-paisen's data,

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:53.720
you'll finally know if you love 
each other or not, right?

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.550
W-We don't know the outcome yet.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:58.410
There you go again.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:02.950
Once it's certain, 
let's have a huge party! Huge!

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:05.320
Why are you so excited? 
It makes no sense at all.

00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:05.320
Let's party!

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.840
Happy things should be 
celebrated all together.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.560
What scientific paper is that written in?

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.580
Kanade-chan, are you going home already?

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.580
Oh, um...

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.110
I suddenly got a shift at 
my part-time job, so...

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.160
Excuse me for leaving first.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.810
She's always rushing around.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:30.080
Does it seem like Kanade-chan has
 been acting strangely, lately?

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:32.330
I wonder if something happened.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:38.610
Shikijou Naoya
This is Shikijou. I'm sorry for
saying what I did so suddenly
the last time we met. Take as
much time as you need to
think about it. And if one day
you let me know your answer,
it would make me very happy.
Thank you.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:39.440
<i>I'm sorry for saying what I did 
so suddenly the last time we met.</i>

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:42.050
<i>Please take as much time as 
you need to think about it.</i>

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:46.100
<i>And if one day you let me know your 
answer, it would make me very happy.</i>

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:51.740
I'm home!

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.080
I'm home, Grandpa.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.130
Oh, Koto-chan. Welcome home.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.340
It's almost time for dinner.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.130
Oh, is it?

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.230
So, you can dodge blows like that one.

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.590
Impressive, Koto-chan.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:16.390
It shows the training I've given 
you since you were young.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.660
Grandpa!

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:21.410
Please don't throw palm strikes 
at me from the moment we meet!

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:24.780
But if you're always training like this,

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:28.240
then you'll be safe even if another 
martial artist attacks sometime.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.020
That will never happen in modern Japan!

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:34.100
I do want to leave out dojo 
to Koto-chan, after all.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:37.030
I'm fine with being a normal girl.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:40.780
...is what she said. She just 
won't take over the dojo from me.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.310
Well, of course. She is a girl, after all.

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:47.570
She got into a really good university.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:52.380
If she can, she should find a 
normal job and get married.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:53.890
That's true.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.920
Are there any good potential 
partners at university?

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:03.180
I'm busy with the lab, so there isn't 
really anyone like that right now.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.880
I see.

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.840
Honestly, this girl.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.220
She got into a department 
where there are lots of men,

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.200
but I haven't caught the 
scent of a man around her.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:15.420
I'd like to see my 
great-grandchildren's faces soon.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.460
Shikijou Naoya
This is Shikijou. I'm sorry for
saying what I did so suddenly
the last time we met. Take as
much time as you need to
think about it. And if one day
you let me know your answer,
it would make me very happy.
Thank you.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:24.460
<i>What is "love," anyway?</i>

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:29.840
<i>At the very least, 
I don't think I love that person.</i>

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.950
<i>I mean, I don't even know 
what kind of person he is.</i>

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:38.100
<i>But if I turn him down, 
I know it will hurt him.</i>

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:44.170
<i>Ever since high school, 
I've been afraid to fall in love.</i>

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:49.000
<i>But I can't stay like this forever.</i>

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.350
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:56.360
Kanade.

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:58.190
Kanade!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.340
Yukimura-senpai!

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:03.500
I-I'm sorry.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.530
I wasn't paying attention.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:07.760
If something is troubling you, tell me.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:14.210
Himuro thinks you've been acting strangely 
lately. She's worried about you.

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.500
Though, I couldn't tell the difference.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.470
So? Are you worried about something?

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.440
<i>It happened to him, too.</i>

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.960
<i>Himuro-senpai 
suddenly confessed her feelings to him, right?</i>

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:30.650
U-Um, Yukimura-senpai.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:33.830
I'd like to consult with 
you about something.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.980
So, what is this consultation about?

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:46.030
This is about a friend.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:51.050
A friend of mine, a girl, 
was suddenly confessed to.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:55.170
It was a boy she'd seen around a few times.

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:58.100
They'd never even spoken, but...

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:01.570
Apparently, he'd fallen in 
love with her at first sight.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.820
And? How did your friend respond?

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.030
She was able to defer her 
reply to a later date...

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.060
but she isn't sure what she should do.

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:14.120
She doesn't think anything 
of the boy in particular...

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:18.820
but she's a little happy that he'd 
fall in love with someone like her.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:21.970
Most of all, very close to her...

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:25.990
there's a couple who share a beautiful love.

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.690
She envies them.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:35.350
And she hopes to one day have 
a beautiful love like that.

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:41.350
But she feels like going out with someone she 
doesn't love for such a reason would be weird.

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:44.250
And...

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:49.780
a long time ago, when she fell 
in love, it failed miserably.

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:53.290
She's worried she might disappoint the boy,

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:56.010
that the same thing might happen again. 
And when she thinks of that...

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:58.610
she gets so scared she can't stand it.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:03.630
But she knows she can't 
stay that way forever.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:06.110
But she's still scared, so...

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.390
She doesn't know what she should do.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.130
<b>Express your Friend's Feelings
through Variables as Below.

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.380
The conversation is tangled, so we will 
correct that by turning it into an equation.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:22.140
<b>I want a beautiful love!
+200 etc...</b>

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.970
Positive feelings are 
assigned positive values.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:25.130
Negative feelings are expressed 
with negative values.

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.020
<b>My past mistakes scare me...
-150 etc...</b>

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:29.140
<b>If the value is greater than 0, date him.</b>

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:29.140
<b>If the value is greater than 0, date him.</b>

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:29.140
If the total is greater than zero, 
she should accept his confession.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:33.150
<i>Why did I go and ask this guy for advice?</i>

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:37.160
By aggregating your friend's feelings 
like this, we can define it thusly.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:38.030
<b>I (reply to confession function) = a + b + c + d + e + f
(if I>0, then accept his confession)</b>

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:41.030
<b>Positive Emotions</b>

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:41.030
<b>Positive Emotions
a = Affection for the boy
b = Happiness at having someone
fall in love with her
c = Wanting to have a beautiful love like that besotted couple
f = Feeling that she can't stay as she is forever</b>

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.950
The positive emotions associated with 
accepting the confession are these.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.790
<b>Negative Emotions</b>

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.790
<b>Negative Emotions
d = Dating someone she doesn't love
for that reason alone is weird
e = Being afraid of making the same mistakes
she made in the past</b>

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.670
And these are the negative emotions 
associated with accepting the confession.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:49.750
<b>Affection for the boy</b>

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:50.400
As she feels nothing in particular for 
the boy, this would be the value of a.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.420
<b>Happiness at having someone fall in love with her</b>

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.810
Then what about b?

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:55.290
How strong is this feeling, 
numerically speaking?

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:56.410
I don't know!

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:00.450
And please don't write out my 
feelings in such a candid way!

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:01.920
It's embarrassing!

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.060
This is about your friend, isn't it?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.620
Yes, it is! It's about my friend!

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:11.560
That's why I don't know the numbers!

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:13.240
Yes, that makes sense.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:17.650
<b>I (reply to confession function)</b>

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.680
Reply to Confession Function!

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.340
What's he talking about, 
"Reply to Confession Function," bear?

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.580
Stop giving stuff fancy names, bear!

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:27.910
<b>(Affection for the boy)</b>

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:27.910
<b>(Happiness at having someone fall in love with her)</b>

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:27.910
<b>(Wanting to have a beautiful love like that besotted couple)</b>

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:27.910
<b>(Dating someone she doesn't love for that reason alone is weird)</b>

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:27.910
<b>(Being afraid of making the same mistakes she made in the past)</b>

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:27.910
<b>(Feeling that she can't stay as she is forever)</b>

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:27.630
This is an overblown formula, 
but it's just simple addition.

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:32.840
The values for each heading are just 
determined by feeling. That's all, bear!

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:42.090
Positive Emotions

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:42.090
Affection for the boy

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:42.090
Happiness at having someone
fall in love with her

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:42.090
Wanting to have a beautiful love
like that besotted couple

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:42.090
Feeling that she can't
stay as she is forever

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:42.090
Negative Emotions

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:42.090
Dating someone she doesn't love

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:42.090
I (reply to confession function) = a + b + c

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:35.560
Which means we don't know the specifics.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.960
The mistakes made in the 
past are unknowns, too.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:42.090
And f, "can't stay like this forever." 
Why is staying as she is bad?

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.650
This is just a guess,

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:46.780
but I think her parents want to 
see their grandchildren's faces.

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:52.590
She wants to be able to fall in love 
so that her parents will worry less.

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:55.850
Really. Your friend is 
very good to her parents.

00:11:58.090 --> 00:11:59.630
Why does that make you feel embarrassed?

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.630
I'm just happy to hear my 
friend being complimented!

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.000
Do you have a problem with that?

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.280
Well, for the time being,

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:09.120
have your friend turn her feelings 
into values and calculate the result.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.180
How can anyone do that?!

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:12.200
It must be done.

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:16.330
If she's been dragging things out and 
still hasn't arrived at a conclusion,

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:23.380
<b>Positive Emotions</b>

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:23.380
<b>Positive Emotions
a = Affection for the boy
b = Happiness at having someone
fall in love with her
c = Wanting to have a beautiful love
like that besotted couple
f = Feeling that she can't
stay as she is forever</b>

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:23.380
<b>Negative Emotions</b>

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:23.380
<b>Negative Emotions
d = Dating someone she doesn't love
for that reason alone is weird
e = Being afraid of making the same mistakes
she made in the past</b>

00:12:16.890 --> 00:12:19.580
then turning her feelings into an equation,

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:23.390
and using those values to decide 
things will be more constructive.

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:27.930
Tell your friend this...

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:31.350
"You are the only one who 
can decide those values."

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:44.280
<i>What is "love," anyway?</i>

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.660
<b>a = Affection for the boy</b>

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:48.270
<i>The way I am right now, 
I don't know the answer.</i>

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.660
<b>e = Being afraid of making the same
mistakes she made in the past</b>

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:50.160
<i>And I'm still scared even now.</i>

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:50.790
<b>f = Feeling that she can't stay 
as she is forever</b>

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:51.790
<b>b = Happiness at having someone 
fall in love with her</b>

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.250
<i>But...</i>

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:52.660
<b>c = Wanting to have a beautiful love 
like that besotted couple</b>

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:56.670
<i>if I take one step forward, 
will something change?</i>

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:04.120
<i>To be honest, I don't know you very well.</i>

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:13.430
Shikijou Naoya
Thank you.
To be honest, I don't know you very well.
 I don't know whether I can fall in love with you,
 or whether I can date you.
 So, could we start as friends first?
 We can start to get to know each other better.
 I'd like to think about it again after that.
 I'm sorry it took me so long to reply.
 Thank you.

00:13:04.120 --> 00:13:08.250
<i>I don't know whether I can fall in love 
with you, or whether I can date you.</i>

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:13.420
<i>So, could we start as friends first?</i>

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.190
Would you like to send this message?

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.190
Cancel

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:18.350
Okay.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.940
<b>(if I>0, then accept his confession)
I = 3</b>

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:27.940
Science Fell in Love,
So I Tried to Prove It [<b>r=1-sinθ</b>]

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:31.880
It's here.

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:35.840
The "proof of love" data 
from that manga artist.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:37.650
It's finally here!

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.180
We'll check the data immediately.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:46.220
The higher the occurrences of 
correlation with this proof,

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.880
the higher the possibility of "love."

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:53.110
<i>The more closely the proof of love 
correlates with my experiences,</i>

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:56.880
<i>the higher the possibility 
that I love Yukimura-kun.</i>

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.940
<i>Please, correlate as much as possible.</i>

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.580
<i>Wait.</i>

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:08.350
<i>Lately, I've had a weird 
hyper-awareness of Ibarada.</i>

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.640
<i>So, the more correlation I 
have with this proof of love,</i>

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:15.730
<i>the higher the possibility 
that I love Ibarada?!</i>

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:17.860
<i>That's the one thing I can't have happen!</i>

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:22.620
First we have pen name 
Niita-san's proof of love.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:25.130
<b>"Niita!-san's Proof of Love"</b>

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:28.630
RikeKoi

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:28.640
<i>I want to show him the things 
I like before anyone else.</i>

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:32.140
<i>When I see him, my heart 
jumps out of my chest.</i>

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:35.390
<i>When nothing is happening, 
he pops into my thoughts.</i>

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:38.380
I see! How lovely!

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:39.990
<i>That applies.</i>

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.220
<i>The second one, "my heart jumps out 
of my chest," hasn't happened, but...</i>

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:45.530
<i>a person would die if that happened, right?</i>

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.110
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:50.310
<i>When I see her, fear makes me jerk backward,</i>

00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:51.920
<i>and when nothing is happening,</i>

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.520
<i>sometimes her annoying face 
pops into my head!</i>

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.540
<b>Heh

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:59.410
Next we have pen name 
Kakitama-san's proof of love.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:01.920
<b>"Kakitama-san's Proof of Love"</b>

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:05.930
<i>When he's with someone of the 
opposite gender, I hate it!</i>

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.880
<i>This is... the degree of jealousy.</i>

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:10.180
<i>This applies, too.</i>

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:12.180
<i>I don't really have this one.</i>

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:16.130
<i>That time at the training camp...</i>

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.440
<i>I got swept up in the moment and snapped...</i>

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:22.010
<i>Does that count for this?!</i>

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:23.930
What's wrong, Kosuke-kun?

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:26.450
I'm moving to the next one.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:28.940
<b>"biwanoshi-san's Proof of Love"</b>

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:33.940
<i>When we're together, even if we don't say 
anything, it doesn't feel oppressive.</i>

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:36.700
<i>It doesn't feel oppressive at all!</i>

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:39.180
It's a little different for me.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:42.460
If neither of us speaks for a while, 
I feel like I have to say something.

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:44.200
For real?

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:46.960
It's even something that doesn't 
work for Himuro-senpai?

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:50.300
I think this depends on 
what stage you're in.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:53.860
Like a relationship that's as comfortable 
and open as a married couple's.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:55.240
Do you think so?

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:57.220
A-A married couple?!

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:58.960
<i>No, I will not accept this.</i>

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:00.980
<i>These feelings are not "love."</i>

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:03.200
<i>They just happened to 
match up with the proof!</i>

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:06.010
<i>I'm sure the next one won't match up at all!</i>

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.980
<b>"Kagari-san's Proof of Love"</b>

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:13.350
<i>I've started thinking about a junior of mine 
that I often have friendly chats with.</i>

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:17.720
<i>But I don't think I'm a good match for him.</i>

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:21.590
<i>So I told myself that 
there was still time...</i>

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.110
<i>"These feelings aren't love."</i>

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:26.760
<i>"This person and I aren't 
suited for each other."</i>

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:28.790
<i>I kept denying my feelings.</i>

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:33.460
<i>But in my continued denial, 
what I realized...</i>

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:38.260
<i>was that every time I denied it, 
it meant I was thinking of him.</i>

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.800
"My proof of love..."

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:44.190
"is that every time I deny 
my feelings by saying I hate him,

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.890
it means I am thinking of him."

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:49.770
"That contradiction within me. 
That's my thinking."

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:53.590
It's heartbreaking, isn't it? 
This person's story.

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.550
<i>This is different, too.</i>

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:58.930
<i>I've never hated Yukimura-kun.</i>

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:00.290
Hm?

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:02.910
Kosuke's died over here.

00:17:03.860 --> 00:17:06.160
What're you doing, Torasuke?

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:08.800
You've been weird lately.

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:10.670
<i>You've gotta be kidding, right?</i>

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:11.800
<i>I seriously have...</i>

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:13.290
<i>For this woman...?</i>

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.410
It can't be true!

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:16.940
Oh, he ran away.

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:20.330
<i>The number of correlations to 
this point are roughly half.</i>

00:17:20.950 --> 00:17:23.320
<i>At the very least, I need a majority.</i>

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:26.180
<i>I want to match the next one.</i>

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:28.690
<b>"Ichina-san's Proof of Love"</b>

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:35.650
<i>I sometimes think of eating, in the sense 
of the food chain, a part of his body.</i>

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:39.210
"And it's precisely because 
I love him so much,

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:42.580
that I want to make him a part of me."

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:45.840
People's mental attitudes really 
are varied, aren't they?

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:52.130
"I love his voice, so I've wanted 
to eat his throat before."

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.970
<i>This does match, but...</i>

00:17:56.970 --> 00:17:59.920
<i>Huh? Is it really all right 
for me to acknowledge that?!</i>

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:03.020
I got chills...

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:05.630
Has my thyroid function gone into overdrive?

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:09.490
There really are so many different 
opinions, aren't there?

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:12.530
They're all telling us very candidly.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:17.000
The proof of love seems to be even more 
wide-ranging than we'd theorized.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:20.120
<i>I can't do this! I don't want to hear any more!</i>

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.310
There're still many more.

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.610
Next we have... Huh?

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.580
What is it, Ibarada? Please continue.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.340
Yes.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:32.130
<b>"Megumi-san's Proof of Love"</b>

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:35.900
<i>When the food I cook with a recipe I'd 
just found turns out deliciously,</i>

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:39.010
<i>he's the first one I want 
to tell to try making it.</i>

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:43.270
<i>When he loses heart, I want to 
think things through with him,</i>

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:46.490
<i>and make it through his troubles together.</i>

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:49.910
<i>And when I'm the one who's lost heart,</i>

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:52.890
<i>I don't want to make him worry about me.</i>

00:18:52.890 --> 00:18:56.350
<i>I want him to always be smiling.</i>

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:03.070
<i>And when I went to his funeral, 
I cried as much as his family did.</i>

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.790
<i>I hadn't noticed that he'd lost heart.</i>

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.340
<i>So, without talking to anyone,</i>

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:11.170
<b>...lost heart
 So, without talking to anyone,
 last week, he took his own life.</b>

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:11.150
<i>last week, he took his own life.</i>

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:17.510
<i>I'm not sure if it's all right for me to 
call circumstances like these proof of love,</i>

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:20.680
<i>but I know I love him.</i>

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:24.620
<i>I hope you'll regard this as the 
excesses of youth and allow it.</i>

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.690
<b>"Kimusei-san's Proof of Love"</b>

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:32.090
<i>On a cold winter's day, she took my hand...</i>

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:37.950
<i>She smiled and said, "My hands are warm, 
aren't they?" and my heart skipped a beat.</i>

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:40.320
<i>It made me want to pull her close to me.</i>

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.240
<i>It made me think, 
"Was she always this cute?"</i>

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:46.450
<b>"Yachou's Proof of Love"</b>

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:49.530
<i>When I have a meal with him, 
everything tastes delicious!</i>

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:52.630
<i>When I hear his voice or see 
him, it makes me feel safe!</i>

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.450
<i>When I hug him, all my fatigue flies away!</i>

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:58.710
<b>"Koruri-san's Proof of Love"</b>

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:02.180
<i>Just getting a text from him makes me grin.</i>

00:20:02.180 --> 00:20:04.500
<i>When I walk, I start skipping.</i>

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:07.190
Just thinking of him warms my heart.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:09.460
Every action and gesture is dear to me.

00:20:09.460 --> 00:20:10.810
I want to hear his voice.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.010
I really want to see him.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:15.040
I end up trying to match the 
kind of person they prefer.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.460
I want to stay near them 
and to give them strength.

00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:17.970
When someone other than me talks 
to them, I get irritated.

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:19.420
When I'm with them, my heart races, but 
I feel comforted at the same time.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.270
When our eyes meet and they 
smile, my heart skips a beat.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.870
My head is full of thoughts 
of her 365 days a year!

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:20.010
I want to spend the night at their house.

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:21.550
I want to touch them and have them touch me.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.530
I want to talk a lot with them.

00:20:23.690 --> 00:20:26.240
This is... incredible.

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:29.890
All of them are forms of "love."

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:33.290
With the love of so many different 
people overflowing...

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:37.260
it's so precious... 
like a tremendous treasure.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:38.950
<i>Honestly.</i>

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:41.510
<i>It's so sparkly, it's infuriating.</i>

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:44.150
<i>Am I worthy of something like this?</i>

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:46.010
<i>I just don't get it!</i>

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:51.470
<i>Will I be able to really fall in 
love with him like these people?</i>

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:53.890
This data is incredibly precious.

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:55.840
We can't let it go to waste.

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:59.100
We will make a complete and thorough 
investigation of this data.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:02.020
And we will discover the 
conditions for love!

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.280
P.N. Samurai Jungle-san
I wonder what might make the other
person happy, and how I might make
that happen. I give serious thought to
the other person.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.280
P.N. Ononokkii-san
After breaking up with the person I was
going out with, I wake crying and screaming
in the middle of the night. Simply thinking of
the other person warms my heart and clears
away my stress. <u>Every action and gesture
is dear to me. </u>I want to have the same
hobbies and interests as the other person.
I just want to see the other person's face,
to hear their voice.

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:27.800
How is it going, Himuro?

00:21:28.160 --> 00:21:29.750
It's difficult.

00:21:30.170 --> 00:21:33.810
It would have been better if each love had 
points of commonality with the others.

00:21:34.070 --> 00:21:35.350
That's impossible.

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:37.060
There's far too great a 
wealth of variety here.

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:40.560
And there are a lot of points 
that seem to match with our own.

00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:43.610
Regardless of what points of 
commonality there may be,

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:47.190
the output of emotion seems to 
vary from person to person.

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:50.250
It may be natural to think of it that way.

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:55.060
By the way, there is one thing 
I've discovered, Yukimura-kun.

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:56.450
What is it, Himuro?

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:57.670
I...

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.990
...am in love with you.

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Next Time

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Proof 6
Science-types Fell in Love, 
So They Tried Not Trying to Prove It.

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:36.920
Next time, Proof 6.

